Common HRIS (Human Resource Information System) platforms include BambooHR, Rippling, Workday, SAP SuccessFactors, ADP Workforce Now, UKG, Gusto, HiBob, Paycor, and Zoho People. There is no standard HRIS software category or certification called "CPAT" ("cpat" usually refers to unrelated terms such as the Candidate Physical Ability Test for firefighters or CPaT Global aviation training software).

Popular HRIS Systems by Category

• Small & Midsize Businesses (SMB): BambooHR, Gusto, Zoho People, HiBob
• Mid-Market & Payroll-Focused: ADP Workforce Now, Paycor, Paylocity, Paycom
• Enterprise & All-in-One: Workday HCM, SAP SuccessFactors, Rippling, UKG
Did you mean a specific HR term or certification (such as SHRM-CP or PHR), or are you looking for HRIS options based on:
• Company size and headcount
• Location (such as India or US payroll compliance)
• Key features (payroll, leave/attendance, performance, or onboarding)

There is no widely known software specifically named "CPAT HRIS," so your search likely refers to one of a few closely related platforms or acronyms:
• PACT HRIS. An all-in-one Human Resource Information System by PACT Software designed to automate employee data, payroll, attendance, leave, and recruitment.
• CPaT Global (LMS). A training and Access Learning Portal used primarily in the aviation industry to manage pilot and crew certifications, compliance, and SCORM training—often integrated alongside a company's main HRIS.
• CPAT (Firefighter Physical Test) & e-HR. The Candidate Physical Ability Test used by fire departments. Some municipal HR departments use electronic HR (e-HR) tracking portals to log candidate scores and application statuses during hiring.
• CPAT Technologies. A software provider offering CPAT WEB for managing vehicle assignments and egress/ingress data points, or pharmaceutical middleware solutions.
